    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n1. **Governance module exports** (`src/finetune/index.js`):\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n   - The test was importing these as named exports but they were only available in the default export\n   - This fixed the `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'join')` error\n\n2. **Toxicity metric signature** (`src/eval/metrics.js`):\n   - Changed function signature from `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references)`\n   - The issue was that `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outs, refs)`, but toxicity was interpreting `references` as `bannedTerms`, causing non-toxic text to be incorrectly flagged\n   - Now the function always uses `defaultBannedTerms` and ignores the references parameter, matching the behavior expected by the test\n\n**Test Results**: All 28 tests passing (8 test files, 0 failures)",
